  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>For Hydrogen like atom,&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi><mo>'</mo></msup></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">=</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><msup><mo>⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;...(i)<br /><br />For Hydrogen atom,&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">=</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;...(ii)<br /><br />Dividing Eqn (ii) by Eqn (i), we get<br /><br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><msup><mtext>RZ</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>or&nbsp;&nbsp;</mtext><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mfrac><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><msup><mo>⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br />According to problem,&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;∴&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mrow><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi><mo>'</mo></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><msup><mo>⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mtext>       </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math><br /><br />The atomic number of Helium atom is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"> <mn>2</mn> </math>. Hence, the required element is Helium.</p>",
